<title>USA: NYC would like clothing sales tax dropped in 1997.</title>
<headline>NYC would like clothing sales tax dropped in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York City, which saw retail sales surge during a one-week experiment with zero sales taxes on clothes in January, was optimistic that Albany will let it start ending these levies in 1997, a city official said.</p>
<p>Deputy Mayor of Operations Randy Mastro said, citing a string of agreements recently reached with Albany lawmakers, &quot;We're hopeful for this year, absolutely.&quot;</p>
</text>
